# The specs crate is built and tested on Windows too, by the workbench that links it
# (a repository of its own, with this one as a submodule), and its tests compare bytes
# of files the repository checks out. They are checked out with the line endings they
# were written with, whatever a Windows clone's `core.autocrlf` says. `text=auto` keeps
# git's own detection of binary files in force.
/sce-specs/** text=auto eol=lf
